WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.300
A French text lands in front of you.

2
00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:03.670
You've never seen it.

3
00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:05.190
Now read it aloud.

4
00:00:05.190 --> 00:00:08.330
Here's one line: «j'aime
aller en ville avec mes amis».

5
00:00:08.330 --> 00:00:09.850
Easy to understand.

6
00:00:09.850 --> 00:00:13.610
But out loud, some slips
only sound a bit foreign.

7
00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:15.470
Others change the meaning.

8
00:00:15.470 --> 00:00:17.910
So how do you sound clear the very first

9
00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:19.570
time you read a text?

10
00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:22.260
In this mission, you'll hear
a model reading of a short

11
00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:24.560
text about a weekend in town.

12
00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:27.160
Then you'll mark up a
text yourself in the lab

13
00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:28.790
and hear it played back.

14
00:00:28.790 --> 00:00:33.170
Your mission: build a routine for
reading any new French text aloud,

15
00:00:33.170 --> 00:00:35.080
and sound clear first time.
